  "title": "Design Temple effectiveness and multi-repository validation",
  "state": "build",
  "owner_position": "developer",
  "assigned_agent_id": "agent-rikku",
  "created_at": "2026-08-31T05:03:14.971Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-08-31T05:13:47.804Z",
  "scope": [
    "Classify the current nonterminal Work Item ledger into release-held, retained-validation, decision-blocked, and planning-parent groups without closing, releasing, or rewriting existing evidence.",
    "Design a bounded local-first experiment that combines a coordinator repository, three service repositories, real Codex task registration, cross-repository contracts, and at least ten completed varied Work Items.",
    "Define truthful measurement, privacy, cost, stop conditions, and later authorization gates before creating repositories, GitHub resources, external CI runs, or implementation tasks."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "The ledger review names every current nonterminal Work Item and recommends an explicit keep, defer, reconcile, or later-decision action without changing its lifecycle.",
    "The validation plan defines repository topology, authority boundaries, participant roles, cross-service scenario, work-item matrix, contract ownership, integration flow, and failure injections.",
    "The measurement protocol separates an instrumentation pilot from any later causal savings claim and defines Token, elapsed-time, context-recovery, overlap, rework, handoff, QA, and completion metrics.",
    "The pilot requires at least ten correctly correlated completed Work Items across multiple task shapes before longitudinal Token or model-routing claims are eligible.",
    "Human approval gates are explicit for external repositories, GitHub writes, hosted CI, material Token or compute cost, sensitive data, and any public or production action.",
    "The planning slice stops with an independently reviewed plan; it creates no service repository, Codex task, GitHub resource, release, deployment, or public artifact."
  ],
